cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  RespSalience: decision-aware contactless pediatric tachypnea screening
message: >-
  If you use this software or the analyses it produces, please cite the
  accompanying manuscript.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hossain
    given-names: Muhammad Imran
    email: muhammadimran.hossain@mail.wvu.edu
    affiliation: West Virginia University
repository-code: 'https://github.com/imranrimon/RespSalience'
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and reproduction artifact for decision-aware
  respiratory screening from RGB video. The proposed model, RespSalience,
  emits a distribution over respiratory rates and forms the tachypnea
  decision by integrating the probability mass above the WHO age threshold,
  rather than regressing a rate and thresholding the point estimate. The
  repository also contains PRISM-Breath, the multimodal regression baseline
  it is compared against, and the analysis code that reproduces every
  quantitative claim in the manuscript.
keywords:
  - respiratory rate
  - tachypnea
  - contactless monitoring
  - pediatric
  - clinical decision support
  - calibration
license: MIT
license-url: 'https://github.com/imranrimon/RespSalience/blob/main/LICENSE'
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Beyond Respiratory-Rate Regression: Decision-Aware Modeling for
      Contactless Pediatric Tachypnea Screening
    authors:
      - family-names: Hossain
        given-names: Muhammad Imran
    status: preprint
